-amount and currency you typed are kept alongside it for reference, but every total
-you ever see is computed in US dollars. This keeps reports consistent even when a
-month mixes several currencies.
+fixed rates in `tally/rates.py` and stores that dollar figure. The original amount
+and currency you typed are kept alongside it for reference, but every total you
+ever see is in US dollars. This keeps reports consistent even when a month mixes
